{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally Gets a Job at a Magazine", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Writing an Article", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling aspects related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The First Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the first conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are two parts to the sentence.<br/><br/>   One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span>.<br/><br/>  Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">will/won't</span><br/> You use a comma after the condition in this form.   You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first. It can be in interrogative form. <br/><br/>  Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Will/Won't</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">if</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  ?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If you don't think about your audience,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you won't engage them.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " A Short Article", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Steps to writing an article.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " STEP 1: Choose your topic<br/><br/>  Select a topic that interests you. Think about your topic over a period of time.<br/> Write a rough draft  with everything you can think of. A rough draft is the first stage in the writing process. It is the stage where you add all your ideas together.<br/><br/>  STEP 2: ADDRESS YOUR AUDIENCE'S NEEDS.<br/><br/>  Think about your audience and how you can write the article to answer their questions.<br/><br/>  STEP 3 : DO YOUR RESEARCH<br/><br/>  Research is very important. Include:  <ul><li>Definitions</li> <li>Quotes</li> <li>Examples</li></ul><br/>  Collect all the important information you need.<br/><br/>  STEP 4: TIGHTEN YOUR DRAFT.<br/><br/>  Put your rough draft and your research together. Does the information in your article blend together? Proofread your work.<br/><br/>  STEP 5<br/><br/> Read the article to a friend. <br/> Does your article:<br/> <ul><li>Include all the information?</li> <li>Is it in logical order?</li></ul><br/> Ensure that the article is checked for spelling, grammar and punctuation errors.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ambitious", "type": "name"}, {"content": "strong desire for success ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I heard you are quite ambitious.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation at work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rough draft", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the first stage of writing before proofreading and adding more information ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Remember, never hand in a rough draft.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to engage", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get and keep someone's attention ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  If you don't know who you are writing for, you won't engage your readers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "accurate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "free from mistakes or errors ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your information will not be accurate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take someone seriously", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to trust someone's work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will not be taken seriously as a writer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write an article on a topic of your choice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose a topic you want to write about. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Decide on your audience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Research your topic. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a 80-100 word article.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your article for spelling, grammar and punctuation errors.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your article aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write an article on a topic of my choice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I complete research on a topic online.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I proofread my work. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my article to a friend.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template